{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898297-alternatives-to-the-beast","id":898297,"title":"Alternatives to the Beast...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-24T15:33:48-07:00","id":898297,"title":"Alternatives to the Beast...","content":"While I may not be the biggest fan of the beast system, while I'm creating this thread as some sort of &quot;What if&quot; scenario but when it comes to Vampires especially the reason why they feed, is there any alternatives to the beast like can the reason for feeding be replaced with something else?<br /> <br /> Like for example Vampires go through mortis stages of decay over time if they don't feed?<br /> <br /> Well point is, I think there could be good examples to come up with alternatives to the beast since I don't think Vampires are required with it to make them Vampires I don't think.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T17:42:14-07:00","id":898439,"title":"","content":"There was an alternative to the beast in the Chronicle Guide, &quot;The Other&quot; iirc. Which was more a calm, disturbing, eldritch and cruel inner self than the raging animal that is the beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T17:44:38-07:00","id":898443,"title":"","content":"Reason for feeding: If you do not feed, you have no Vitae. No Vitae, no waking up. You either feed, or go into a coma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T18:14:06-07:00","id":898454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898297-alternatives-to-the-beast?p=898443#post898443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reason for feeding: If you do not feed, you have no Vitae. No Vitae, no waking up. You either feed, or go into a coma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Torpor?<br /> <br /> Well one possibility that once you go in a coma or torpor, your body goes through corpse like decay until you're literally a skeleton until someone sprays blood on you which you'll awakened from torpor as a walking skeleton with fangs and feed those nearby to restore your original appearance (think about Frank and Julia from the first two Hellraiser movies where they're skinless until restoring fully when they feed). Well think of the beginning of Lords of Shadow 2 or in Bram Stoker's Dracula where he's a decrepit old man but when he feeds, he restores his youthful appearance.<br /> <br /> Is such a thing possible Requiem? Or maybe once again saved for a Bloodline where their main weakness when they don't feed, they decay like a corpse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-24-2016, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T18:49:50-07:00","id":898476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898297-alternatives-to-the-beast?p=898454#post898454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Torpor?<br /> <br /> Well one possibility that once you go in a coma or torpor, your body goes through corpse like decay until you're literally a skeleton until someone sprays blood on you which you'll awakened from torpor as a walking skeleton with fangs and feed those nearby to restore your original appearance (think about Frank and Julia from the first two Hellraiser movies where they're skinless until restoring fully when they feed). Well think of the beginning of Lords of Shadow 2 or in Bram Stoker's Dracula where he's a decrepit old man but when he feeds, he restores his youthful appearance.<br /> <br /> Is such a thing possible Requiem? Or maybe once again saved for a Bloodline where their main weakness when they don't feed, they decay like a corpse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires in general look dead when they go into torpor. Vitae from a more powerful vampire can wake them early, but if you aren't killed you stay in torpor for a period depending on your Humanity.<br /> <br /> I don't see how this would really affect your game, however. Vampires don't want to go into torpor, it is like being in a coma, you fall into it when you're starved or beaten. Vampires can survive for a long time in torpor, and it's good for 'time skips,' but otherwise having special rules for being in torpor would be like having special rules for being in a coma, complete with rumors of mystic dream journeys.<br /> <br /> It's not something with them constantly like the Beast or the Other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T21:05:07-07:00","id":898580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898297-alternatives-to-the-beast#post898297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I may not be the biggest fan of the beast system, while I'm creating this thread as some sort of &quot;What if&quot; scenario but when it comes to Vampires especially the reason why they feed, is there any alternatives to the beast like can the reason for feeding be replaced with something else?<br /> <br /> Like for example Vampires go through mortis stages of decay over time if they don't feed?<br /> <br /> Well point is, I think there could be good examples to come up with alternatives to the beast since I don't think Vampires are required with it to make them Vampires I don't think.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wouldnt this be like a human choosing not to eat?? Eventually we would wither up and die.<br /> <br /> Vampires need to feed. As mentioned. If you dont feed, you will eventually just not wake up one night. No vitae is a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T22:10:38-07:00","id":898632,"title":"","content":"I would imagine Torpor would be a pretty strong incentive. You don't die from starvation, you just collapse into a coma and are forced to replay your memories on an endless loop until you wake up. Which can take anywhere from several hours to many centuries depending on the individual. Or, if you're unable to muster the will to wake up, you have to wait for the day somebody force feeds you blood.<br /> <br /> And you don't start to decay in torpor, your body just starts to mummify. In time, you'll appear sunken and shriveled. But once you get some fresh blood, you'll rejuvenate yourself back to the point before death.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's assuming somebody doesn't dig up your body and expose it to sunlight because they think you're just a regular corpse.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, the threat of catatonia should be more than enough to keep a vampire looking for their next meal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-25-2016, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T22:40:07-07:00","id":898657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898297-alternatives-to-the-beast#post898297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I may not be the biggest fan of the beast system, while I'm creating this thread as some sort of &quot;What if&quot; scenario but when it comes to Vampires especially the reason why they feed, is there any alternatives to the beast like can the reason for feeding be replaced with something else?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lots of people have addressed why vampires don't need the Beast at all to desire to feed.<br /> <br /> I'm curious why you mean by not being a fan of, &quot;the beast system.&quot; What does that even mean? While the Beast is a prominent element of Requiem vampires, there's extremely few rules that are explicitly rules that govern the Beast instead of reference it: Predatory Aura/Lashing Out, and Frenzies. What other systems are there that you don't like, and what don't you like about those two systems?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well point is, I think there could be good examples to come up with alternatives to the beast since I don't think Vampires are required with it to make them Vampires I don't think.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Lots of things in Requiem aren't &quot;required&quot; to make vampires. Vampires are a mythological creature it a hugely diverse concept of what makes a vampire. The inclusion of the Beast in Requiem is to make a specific kind of vampire (notably to heighten the struggle between maintaining a character's past humanity, and the draw to become the predator they have been turned into; which is a staple of plenty of source material).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T23:23:39-07:00","id":898693,"title":"","content":"It's pretty clear from spaceharrier72's posts that they don't want to play a game where the protagonists are morally reprehensible monsters. They don't like the Beast because it occasionally forces them to engage in monstrous actions whether they intend to or not.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11735\" data-vbnamecard=\"11735\">spaceharrier72</a>, I'm sure it's possible to excise these elements you find distasteful from the game, but the books are going to be fighting you at every turn. Vampire is designed from the ground up as a game of personal horror - a game where you play as the monsters, and the horror arises from within your character, rather than without. If you don't mind doing a lot of legwork, you can certainly ignore those themes. But it might also be worth considering that this might just not be the game for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T06:59:57-07:00","id":898883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898297-alternatives-to-the-beast?p=898693#post898693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty clear from spaceharrier72's posts that they don't want to play a game where the protagonists are morally reprehensible monsters. They don't like the Beast because it occasionally forces them to engage in monstrous actions whether they intend to or not.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11735\" data-vbnamecard=\"11735\">spaceharrier72</a>, I'm sure it's possible to excise these elements you find distasteful from the game, but the books are going to be fighting you at every turn. Vampire is designed from the ground up as a game of personal horror - a game where you play as the monsters, and the horror arises from within your character, rather than without. If you don't mind doing a lot of legwork, you can certainly ignore those themes. But it might also be worth considering that this might just not be the game for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'll admit I'm kinda interested on the whole &quot;Other&quot; concept that Milo mentioned about since it might be suited for me better than the beast it seems due to the fact I don't wish to play as something with a walking time bomb temper but rather as a calm &amp; collected character with a tranquil fury (I think that's what the &quot;Other&quot; is about I think) but thing is though I kinda prefer just playing the simple concept of a undead corpse maintaining their immortality through blood though with no other things shoehorned in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-25-2016, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T07:15:04-07:00","id":898890,"title":"","content":"Check out CJ Carellas's Witchcraft RPG. Their vampires may be more to your style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T07:30:43-07:00","id":898901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898297-alternatives-to-the-beast?p=898890#post898890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out CJ Carellas's Witchcraft RPG. Their vampires may be more to your style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although the Vampires in Witchcraft aren't exactly sanguine types since they feed on essence released by strong emotions which rather sounds new agey.<br /> <br /> Wait a minute...I've read a review and it said that the Mystery Codex has rules for Sanguine/Blood Drinking Vampires so I guess it solves that problem...maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-25-2016, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:00:52-07:00","id":898924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898297-alternatives-to-the-beast?p=898901#post898901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although the Vampires in Witchcraft aren't exactly sanguine types though I've heard.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be with the right drawback, its just not default and its very easy to just make it default if you want. That being said, if you want to get further away from the monster/beast/abuser angle, not having to drink people's blood is a good place to start.<br /> <br /> Also the rpg Angel (also from Eden Studios) might be the vampires you want. Their default is that vamps are souless monsters, but PCs are special in that they are not. <br /> <br /> Based on what you have written, I am suspecting Requiem is not the Vampire game you are looking for since it plays very heavily on items that you dislike. Even items like, lets get rid of clans is less core to the game than what your concerns are.<br /> <br /> The Other concept is basically the same thing as Frenzy, its just being cold, calculating and without morals or mercy as opposed to being animalistic, impulsive and without morals or mercy. Its calmly drinking from a mortal until they are dead rather than ravenously doing so. If players want to play their beast that way its cool by me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:05:05-07:00","id":898928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898297-alternatives-to-the-beast?p=898883#post898883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but thing is though I kinda prefer just playing the simple concept of a undead corpse maintaining their immortality through blood though with no other things shoehorned in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so you like the immortal aspect of vampires. You like the feeding aspect of vampires. You want to replace Frenzy with some other negative aspect that still encourages feeding, but not at the cost of pure player-agency (i.e. loss of control).<br /> <br /> Then yes, I think your previous idea of tying health/immortality to feeding could be a reasonable substitute. Some things you should think about<b></b>:<ul><li>Frenzy/The Beast is an inherent theme in the game. It's tough to avoid it entirely, and a lot of powers and effects will be taking it into account. Be prepared to do a lot of bookeeping to scrub them from the mechanics. From the Bestial, Wanton, Competitive conditions. From Coil of the Wyrm. From lashing out against Majesty as a defense. There will be a lot of little things you are going to have to decide on the fly when you encounter them.</li> <li>Frenzy/The Beast is something that while not automatically present in every scene is a <i>potential </i>in every scene. It is kind of the Wandering Monster of V:tR. If you aren't deliberately replacing the Beast with something that has the potential of triggering in any given scene, you are making your custom vampire template more powerful, or less disadvantaged, than stock. Account for that.</li> </ul>Replacing the Beast with some kind of Degeneration means replacing the more overt Predatory themes of the game with something else. In this case, I'd probably suggest Isolation. The vampire should feel the call of immortality and this is what separates them from humans. This should probably come in multiple forms. Examples:<ul><li>Any evening where the kindred does not spend 1 vitae to 'wake' their immortal form, they revert to both the state of the corpse (wounds) and the actual age (Older vampires look more decrepit, etc.) of their true form. Appropriate wound and social penalties would apply to all actions.</li> <li>Ramp up the Social Penalties of low Humanity, or avoid ways for the Kindred to circumvent those penalties. Reframe the perception of them into that alien, not human feeling more than as a wolf among the herd.</li> <li>Recast feeding grounds as less about territorial predators, and more about having one's own space to truly feel alone amongst the crowd.</li> <li>Find a way to simulate a mental condition or theme to replace how frenzy triggers encourage direct, animalistic conflict between Kindred and their opponents / loved ones. Maybe people / other Kindred who see your 'true self' receive bonuses in actions against you, or you receive penalties to actions against them. These penalties can only be removed by feeding from them or some other similar, theme reinforcing manner.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:52:35-07:00","id":898969,"title":"","content":"I don't think frenzy was meant to be a mechanic to force you to drink blood. The rules for frenzy predate the amount of Vitae impacting your frenzy rolls.<br /> <br /> I think the thought was as follows and mind you its only my opinion from the Masquerade 1st edition days (1991):<br /> 1. RPG players play heroes. We need to have a mechanic in there that makes them perform non-heroic acts since these are vampires.<br /> 2. If Humanity is mental/soul hit points (which in some respects it is), players will never do anything that threatens them losing these hit points as it will be suboptimal. We would get a game about vampires where everyone acts like saints, even moreso than Lawful Good characters.<br /> <br /> Now I am not a fan of viewing humanity as mental hit points, losing and gaining them are the major part of the game thematically. That one game where a player bought her Humanity up to 2 was a major wake up call as to how far afield that Daeva has gone. Frenzy was meant to put your Humanity at risk. I think since then, it has taken on other significance within the game.<br /> <br /> At that point in time, there were few vampire stories where the vampires flew off the rails and went crazy so it was not from a literary source (I still don't know many). I mean they got angry and flashed fangs and a lot of them were just straight evil, but nothing to the level of a Frenzy. Raging out is something werewolves do in literature.<br /> <br /> The fact that animating your body, healing damage and using your powers requires Vitae expenditure is what is suppose to force you to drink blood, mostly the first one.<br /> <br /> Thats all separate form not wanting Frenzy in your games. If you remove Frenzy, you don't need to replace it with something else that makes you want to feed. You need to replace it with something that puts your Humanity at risk or not depending on how you feel about the Humanity stat and what the expectations are for it going up and down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:23:07-07:00","id":898999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898297-alternatives-to-the-beast?p=898969#post898969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think frenzy was meant to be a mechanic to force you to drink blood. The rules for frenzy predate the amount of Vitae impacting your frenzy rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like a lot of your points, but since 2E V:tM on at least - which is the majority of the game popularity and lifetime - Frenzy was billed as a mechanical system which forced you to fight, to flee, or to feed. 2E Requiem has scaled this back, in my opinion, but the mechanics seem to me about loss of control in stressful situations, leading to a few, brutal reactions. And yeah - you have to go waaaay back to remove the concept of blood/feeding from frenzy results.<br /> <br /> You can say that's just one aspect of frenzy and not the primary aspect, and I'd agree, but it's a system which demands a certain action, and removes player agency for doing other actions while under the mechanical effects. So, almost regardless of original intent, frenzy is directly a mechanic which <i>forces </i>Kindred to drink blood. Healing, disciplines and physical intensity are all mechanical systems which encourage it - but a given character can opt out. Not the same as the frenzy rules, at the very least being much harder to opt out from - via Willpower, pricey disciplines, Merit Styles, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:42:07-07:00","id":899026,"title":"","content":"I think we are all forgetting some major points here... <br /> <br /> Vampires do not have to be Morally reprehensible monsters. <br /> <br /> If you dont want to frenzy, build up high resolve composure to justify that you are cool and collected. Keep well fed. Then failing the frenzy checks will be minimal. <br /> <br /> If all of your protagonists are morally reprehensible monsters and you dont like it, perhaps find different people to play with. Not everyone who creates a vampire makes these evil horrible monsters. Sure this game is about personal horror, but what is that? Your personal horror might be different than mine. I have played 2 games with 2 different story tellers and the game theme ended up being about love. Finding relationships and keeping humanity. Slice of life. Sure, bad shit happened, but that didnt mean that my characters ran around murdering, raping and pillaging everything I saw. In one of them, my vampire became sort of a vampire hunter who hunted down the &quot;monsters&quot; There are a lot of different ways to play this game...<br /> <br /> <br /> But after reading so many of your posts where you want to change vampires fundamentally, I am beginning to wonder if this is the right game for you. You could play a dungeons and dragons vampire. No beasts, no frenzy. but This one if you take out crucial things, What is left? If humanity is gone, touchstones are gone. if you take out the beast, all disciplines would go because they are meant to be extensions of the beast. Lashing out would be gone. You would simply have an immortal human who drinks blood here and there. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> side note: Humanity is not mental hit points and sometimes you hit breaking points when you dont want to. So even if you do act like a saint, you still could lose your humanity. It is just about accepting the beast inside of you. Accepting that you are no longer human. Huge threads discussing this one. Not everyone seems to agree on what this is....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T10:24:35-07:00","id":900169,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Hey folks, just letting everyone know the user who started this thread, along with the two recently quarantined threads was a dummy account for a user who had previously been permanently banned. The new account has been banned as well.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}